/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/events.md:459:For model-invoked calls the terminal `tool` event is published when the turn's tool batch durably commits, not the instant execution finishes — a tool whose batch is interrupted before commit never publishes its terminal event, matching the durable outcome. `shell()` publishes immediately. `shell()` per-call `env` values are redacted to `<redacted>` in the recorded arguments (keys stay visible); a failed `shell()` carries an error-shaped result whose `details.exitCode` is `-1`.
