/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-666-- `fetch` — custom fetch implementation for the transport.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md:667:- `timeoutMs` — per-request timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to the MCP SDK default (60 seconds).
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md:668:- `resetTimeoutOnProgress` — reset the per-request timeout whenever the server sends a progress notification. Default `false`.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-669-- `tools` — allowlist of tools to adapt, by the server's own tool names, in this order. Unknown, repeated, and task-required names reject the connection.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-670-- `optional` — let the agent run without this server when it fails to resolve. Default `false`: a failed connection fails the submission before the model runs. With `optional: true`, any resolve failure mounts zero tools for the submission instead — announced to the model as a [`resources` signal](#dynamic-resources) and to observers as a `log`-level warning event — and the next submission retries.
