/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-693-- Tool discovery follows `tools/list` pagination; a repeated cursor throws. Tools that require task-based execution are skipped with a console warning (allowlisting one is an error).
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-694-- `auth` resolves before every request; a 401 re-resolves once and retries, so a credential the application has already refreshed recovers in place.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md:695:- A tool result's content is flattened to text for the model; a result with `isError` becomes a tool error. When the server declares an output schema, the MCP client validates structured content against it and a mismatch is an error.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md-696-- The adapted definitions are complete — do not wrap them in `defineTool()`.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/reference/agent-api.md:697:- `close()` closes the underlying MCP client connection; call it during application shutdown. On any connection or discovery failure, the client is closed before the error propagates. (Hook-declared connections are runtime-owned — the runtime closes them.)
