/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/schedules.md:68:Cadence and timezone belong to the cron library: croner takes a standard five-field cron pattern (with an optional seconds field), an IANA `timezone` option, `protect: true` to skip a fire while the previous callback is still running, and a `catch` handler for callback errors. Any in-process scheduler works the same way — the only Flue-specific part is the `dispatch(...)` call.
