/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/schedules.md-151-The `read()` promise is not itself durable: if the process dies mid-await, the run still settles, but anything after the `await` is gone — so side effects that must not be lost belong inside the agent (a tool call), not after the read. For orchestration that must survive crashes, see [Workflows](/docs/guide/workflows/#durable-workflows).
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/schedules.md-152-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/schedules.md:153:For schedules that live outside a Flue application entirely — a standalone cron script on another machine — boot the runtime with [`start()`](/docs/guide/building-agents/#standalone-scripts) and use the same handle.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/schedules.md-154-
