/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/sandboxes.md-176-A sandbox factory may also carry a `tools` function. When present, it **replaces** the framework's default model-facing tool set for that agent — an adapter for an exec-less environment, for example, keeps the `read`/`write`/`edit` file tools but swaps the shell-backed `bash`/`grep`/`glob` for its own executor tool. Adapters compose these sets from the exported per-tool factories (`createReadTool`, `createBashTool`, and friends) rather than rebuilding from scratch. Because capabilities vary this way, check an integration's documentation before assuming ordinary file or command tools are available. See the [Sandbox Adapter API](/docs/reference/sandbox-api/) for the contract.
