/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/cli/run.md-15-`flue run` executes one agent module in the local Node.js process: it submits one message, streams the agent's activity to stderr, prints the final assistant reply to stdout, and exits. No server is created and no build artifacts are written — only the agent module (and whatever it imports) is loaded, never `app.ts`. A module that imports `cloudflare:*` APIs fails with a pointer at `vite dev`, where platform bindings exist.
