/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/observability.md-99-Usage also rolls up at coarser boundaries: `operation` and `compaction` events carry aggregate usage for the work they bound. When summing usage across events, sum one level only — `turn` values are the leaves, and the roll-ups already include them. Duration values at different levels overlap the same way and should not be added together. Inside the agent, `useResponseFinish()` receives the whole response's aggregate usage — the right place to stamp token counts onto response metadata for your client; see [Event hooks](/docs/guide/agent-hooks/#event-hooks).
