/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/tools.md-161-- **Everything effectful goes in a step.** Code between steps re-executes on recovery, so keep it cheap and effect-free — derive values, branch, loop.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/tools.md-162-- **Names identify the work.** Derive them deterministically (`seed:${project.name}`), never from randomness or timing. Reusing a name within one call throws.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/tools.md:163:- **Values are JSON and should stay small.** Store large artifacts in the sandbox and record a pointer.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/tools.md-164-- **Steps are exactly-once-recorded, at-least-once-executed.** A crash in the narrow window between a step finishing and its record landing re-runs that one step, so steps around external effects should be individually idempotent.
