/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/routing.md-133-## Protecting your agents
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/routing.md-134-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/routing.md:135:A mounted agent has no built-in authentication: **anyone who can reach a conversation URL can talk to that conversation** — send it messages, read its full history, abort its work. There is no per-agent middleware export either. Treat a mount like any other sensitive endpoint and protect it with your application's normal middleware, layered in `app.ts` before the mount it applies to.
