/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/channels.md-123-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/channels.md:124:`initialData` is recorded once, when the dispatch creates the conversation, and ignored by every later send. It carries the facts that define what the conversation _is_ — the thread, the repository, the ticket — as opposed to what each message _says_. When the agent declares an `initialData` schema static, the value is validated at admission, so a creating dispatch that omits or malforms it fails instead of seeding a broken conversation. See [Passing data to the agent](/docs/guide/agent-hooks/#passing-data-to-the-agent).
