/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-6-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:7:This guide migrates a Flue codebase from `1.0.0-beta.9` to Flue 2. It is written for working beta applications: every section pairs the beta API with its replacement, and the [checklist](#migration-checklist) at the end orders the work.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-8-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-9-The release is a breaking version upgrade and major redesign of core internal architecture. Five conceptual changes drive the upgrade:
--
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-19-## Before you start: persisted state resets
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-20-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:21:The current release stores Flue schema **version 8**; the beta stored version 5. Pre-1.0 persisted schemas are **reset-only** — the runtime rejects an older database before any application code runs, and there is no in-place migration.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-22-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:23:- If beta conversation state is disposable, plan a drained deployment: retire the old agents (on Cloudflare, with `deleted_classes` migrations) and create fresh ones. Application data that shares an agent's storage (a `base`/`wrap` DO extension, values written beside Flue's tables) is deleted with it — export anything you need first.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-24-- If beta state must survive, export it through the beta application _before_ upgrading, and re-seed after.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-25-
--
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-51-- The `root` and `output` fields are retired — Vite owns both. Strict validation rejects them everywhere except `flue run`, which silently drops unknown keys — delete them.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-52-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:53:`.env` loading also changed: `vite dev` loads Vite's standard `.env` files, and `flue run` loads `.env` (pass `--env` for an alternate). Built servers never load `.env`.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-54-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-55-## Routing: the auto-router is gone
--
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-78-```
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-79-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:80:- `createAgentRouter(fn)` is a pure router factory serving `POST /:id`, `GET|HEAD /:id`, `POST /:id/abort`, and `GET /:id/attachments/:attachmentId` relative to the mount. URL shapes are yours — keep the old `/agents/<name>` paths if deployed clients address them.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-81-- **Registration comes from the [`'use agent'` scan](/docs/guide/building-agents/#use-agent-directive), not the mount.** A dispatch-only agent stays unmounted and still works; mounting registers nothing.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:82:- The agent-module `export const route` and `export const attachments` conventions are deleted. Per-agent middleware becomes ordinary Hono middleware registered before the mount; attachment download exists on every mounted agent.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-83-- The `POST /:id` body changed: `{ "message": "...", "images": [...] }` becomes a bare message object — `{ "message": { "kind": "user", "body": "..." } }` — with optional top-level `initialData` and `uid`. The `?wait` query is gone; clients follow the returned `streamUrl` or use the SDK's `wait()`.
