/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-216-- The named-string form (`dispatch({ agent: 'name', ... })`) is removed — pass the agent function itself.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md:217:- The creation seed field is **`initialData`** (validated by the agent's `initialData` schema static at creation, read with `useInitialData()`; ignored on sends that continue an existing instance). If your beta app abused the first message body to carry setup facts, move them here.
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-218-- **`uid` send conditions**: omit to continue-or-create; pass a previous receipt's `uid` to continue only that incarnation (`AgentInstanceNotFoundError`/404 otherwise); pass `null` to create only (`AgentInstanceExistsError`/409 otherwise, carrying the existing uid). Conditions are checked at admission and create nothing on failure. `getAgentInstance(agent, id)` looks up `{ id, uid }` without sending.
