/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-243-
/home/ubuntu/.npm/_npx/8cba94e94504a6dc/node_modules/@flue/runtime/docs/guide/migration.md-244-- `registerProvider('ollama', { api, baseUrl, ... })` — now `setProvider(createProvider({ id: 'ollama', auth, models, api }))` with Pi's `createProvider`. Models are declared as full `Model` objects (each carries its own `baseUrl` and metadata); there is no catalog hydration or zero-fill for custom providers. The [Ollama recipe](/docs/guide/models/#custom-providers) is the template.
